{# Home-screen icon, tab favicon and manifest, shared by every page's <head>.
   Paths are relative like the rest of the site (it is served from a
   project-pages subpath). Deliberately NO apple-mobile-web-app-capable: an iOS
   standalone web app keeps its own storage, separate from Safari, so the
   emailed sign-in link (which opens in Safari) could never sign the reader in
   there. Without it, the home-screen icon is a shortcut into Safari and keeps
   the sign-in the reader already has. See tests/test_home_screen_icon.py. #}
<link rel="icon" href="assets/icons/favicon.svg" type="image/svg+xml"/>
<link rel="apple-touch-icon" href="assets/icons/apple-touch-icon.png"/>
<link rel="manifest" href="manifest.webmanifest"/>
<meta name="apple-mobile-web-app-title" content="Momentum"/>
<meta name="theme-color" content="#f1ecdf" media="(prefers-color-scheme: light)"/>
<meta name="theme-color" content="#17150F" media="(prefers-color-scheme: dark)"/>
